// F1 negative: expected-type instantiation makes a generic function VALUE precisely checked, so a
// shape that cannot line up with the expectation is a static E0007 instead of a runtime surprise.
// `first` instantiates against `map`'s expected `(int) -> _` parameter, but its own parameter is a
// `List<T>` — an `int` element can never flow into it. Both the value's own subsumption (at the
// reference) and the call's argument check (at the method name) report the mismatch.
// expect: error E0007 at 12:17
// expect: error E0007 at 12:6
// expect: exit 1
fn first<T>(xs: List<T>): T {
    return xs[0];
}
echo [1, 2].map(first);
